# Testing and verification

- Add a regression test for each bug fix when practical.
- Test observable behavior, important branches, and failure modes; avoid tests
  that only restate mocks or inflate coverage.
- Run checks proportional to risk, including applicable format, lint,
  typecheck, test, dead-code, package/artifact, and build validation.
- Fix failures caused by the change; do not weaken checks to make them pass.
- Report commands and results accurately, including checks not run and why.
- Treat green CI as evidence, not a substitute for engineering judgment.
